From 836296de09aa0e0be9ae6668a29cddb28aa48bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 11:51:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(profile): rebuild Progression to match the reference
 mockup exactly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Level card redesigned: gradient tinted by level color, NIVEAU/name
  left, XP total right, progress bar with min/pct/next labels below
- New Badges grid (3x2): 6 badges computed from REAL profile stats
  (streak, QCM success rate, forum posts, contests completed, level
  thresholds) — not the mockup's static/fake badge list
- New Barème grid: pulls the actual admin-configured XP economy from
  GET /settings/bareme (direct-answer bonus, hint penalties, forum
  XP) instead of hardcoding numbers that could drift from reality
- Removed the old checklist + full level ladder from this section:
  the checklist duplicated the separate 'Missions du jour' card
  added earlier, and the ladder isn't part of the reference mockup's
  dedicated Progression view (still shown at the top of the profile
  page in the smaller level-progress header, unchanged)
